        "path": "media/gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-3-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of chicken breast strips frying in pale pan",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the Gousto recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "number": 4,
      "heading": "Add the spices",
      "blocks": [
        "Add the onion and cook 3–4 minutes until softened. Stir in the ginger, garlic, tomato paste, garam masala, curry powder and a pinch of salt and cook 1–2 minutes until fragrant."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Add the spices · 3–4 min",
          "seconds": [
            180,
            240
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "timer-2",
          "label": "Add the spices · 1–2 min",
          "seconds": [
            60,
            120
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-4",
        "path": "media/gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-4-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of chicken and spiced onion browning",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the Gousto recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-5",
      "number": 5,
      "heading": "Simmer the curry",
      "blocks": [
        "Dissolve the stock mix in {{stock-water}} boiled water. Stir it and the chopped tomatoes into the pan, bring to a boil, then reduce to medium-low for 10–12 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the chicken is cooked through with no pink meat."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Simmer the curry",
          "seconds": [
            600,
            720
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-5",
        "path": "media/gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-5-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of chicken strips in red tomato curry sauce",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the Gousto recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-6",
      "number": 6,
      "heading": "Wilt the spinach",
      "blocks": [
        "Wash the spinach in a colander, pour boiling water over it until it wilts, rinse under the cold tap and squeeze out excess water."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [],
      "image": {
        "id": "gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-6",
        "path": "media/gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-6-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of wilted spinach in colander",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the Gousto recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-7",
      "number": 7,
      "heading": "Finish the curry and rice",
      "blocks": [
        "Finely chop the coriander including stalks. Mix half into the rice with a pinch of salt. Stir the wilted spinach and half the yoghurt into the thickened curry."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [],
      "image": {
        "id": "gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-7",
        "path": "media/gousto-chicken-tikka-masala-7-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of pot of brown rice with chopped coriander",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the Gousto recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-8",
      "number": 8,
      "heading": "Serve",
      "blocks": [
        "Serve the curry over the coriander rice with the remaining yoghurt and coriander."
